+# Phase 8b Code Review — STORY-013: Target Pricing Sync
+
+**Date:** 2026-05-01
+**Branch:** `story-013/story-013`
+**PR:** [#8 — feat(STORY-013): Target pricing sync per-item PUT with queue](https://github.com/hpi-gorillacommerce/api-retail-target/pull/8)
+**Reviewers:** architect, skeptic, simplifier, rule-reviewer, qa-preflight (parallel sub-agents)
+**Verdict:** ✅ APPROVED with auto-fixes applied (commit `7d4d9af`)
+
+---
+
+## Summary
+
+Phase 8 delivered a complete in-memory implementation of the pricing queue, worker, router, and client. All 61 tests were GREEN at phase-8 close. Five sub-agents reviewed in parallel; findings were synthesized and Critical/High/Medium fixes were applied before this report was written.
+
+**Final state: 61/61 tests GREEN after all auto-fixes.**
+
+---
+
+## Auto-Fixed Findings (committed `7d4d9af`)
+
+### 🔴 CRITICAL — Fixed
+
+**C-1: `dequeue_next()` ignored `next_retry_at` — backoff was stored but never enforced**
+- File: `app/pricing/queue.py`
+- Issue: The dequeue loop matched any `status == "failed"` row regardless of `next_retry_at`. Exponential backoff was computed and written to the DB but immediately bypassed — failed items were retried at full 1 req/s rate.
+- Fix: Added `now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)` gate: failed rows are only eligible when `next_retry_at is None or next_retry_at <= now`. Also added `_force_retry_eligible(queue_id)` test helper (simulates clock advancing in tests without real sleep).
+- Test impact: Three tests relied on the broken behavior (`test_backoff_increases_with_retry_count`, `test_backoff_capped_at_300_seconds`, `test_retry_exhaustion_dead_letters_not_deletes`). Updated to use `_force_retry_eligible()` between `process_one()` calls. `test_backoff_capped_at_300_seconds` now also asserts the computed backoff is within the 300s cap.
+
+---
+
+### 🟠 HIGH — Fixed
+
+**H-1: `_lock = threading.Lock()` — dead import and dead variable**
+- File: `app/pricing/queue.py`
+- Issue: `threading` was imported and `_lock` was assigned at module level but never acquired anywhere. Implied thread safety that didn't exist.
+- Fix: Removed `import threading` and `_lock`. Added module docstring explaining the production safety contract (SELECT FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED replaces locking in the Postgres backend).
+
+**H-4: Worker caught httpx exceptions that can never reach it**
+- File: `app/pricing/worker.py`
+- Issue: `HttpTargetPricingClient.update_price()` already converts `httpx.TimeoutException`, `httpx.ConnectError`, `httpx.HTTPError` to `PriceUpdateResult`. The worker's `except (httpx.TimeoutException, ...)` block was dead code. `import httpx` in the worker was a leaky coupling.
+- Fix: Replaced with `except Exception` safety net (catches unexpected protocol violations from any `TargetPricingClient` implementation). Removed `import httpx`.
+
+**H-5 (Rule Violation): Write endpoints not feature-flagged per MOCK_ONLY_DIRECTIVE**
+- File: `app/pricing/router.py`, `app/core/config.py`
+- Issue: MOCK_ONLY_DIRECTIVE requires all write endpoints to be feature-flagged off until a go-live story enables them. `POST /enqueue` and `POST /dead-letters/{id}/retry` were unconditionally registered.
+- Fix: Added `enable_pricing_writes: bool = False` to `Settings` (env var `ENABLE_PRICING_WRITES`). Both write endpoints now `Depends(_require_writes_enabled)` which raises HTTP 503 when the flag is off.
+
+---
+
+### 🟡 MEDIUM — Fixed
+
+**M-2: 404 response in `GET /status/{product_id}` was not RFC 7807**
+- File: `app/pricing/router.py`
+- Issue: Returned `{"detail": "Product not found"}` — missing `type`, `title`, `status` fields and wrong content-type.
+- Fix: Returns `JSONResponse(status_code=404, media_type="application/problem+json", content={"type": "/problems/not-found", "title": "Not Found", "status": 404, "detail": ...})`.
+
+**M-3: `offer_price` cross-field constraint missing**
+- File: `app/pricing/schemas.py`
+- Issue: Spec requires `offer_price <= list_price` when offer_price is set. Missing validation meant invalid data entered the queue and would dead-letter on first PUT to Target.
+- Fix: Added `@model_validator(mode="after")` checking `offer_price <= list_price`. Validator also caught a pre-existing test data bug (burst test was creating items with `offer_price=17.99 > list_price=10.99`).
+
+**M-4: No history written for intermediate (non-final) retry failures**
+- File: `app/pricing/worker.py`
+- Issue: History was only recorded on success, permanent failure, and dead-letter. Intermediate retryable failures (429, 5xx before max_retries) left no audit trail.
+- Fix: Added `record_history(..., outcome="transient_error")` before `mark_failed()` in both the exception path and the HTTP retryable path. Now all attempts are auditable.
+
+---
+
+### 🔵 LOW — Fixed
+
+**L-1: `datetime`/`Decimal` imported inside `_serialize()` on every call**
+- File: `app/pricing/router.py`
+- Fix: Moved to module-level imports.
+
+---
+
+## Deferred Findings (pre-staging required)
+
+These are not blocking for merge but MUST be resolved before production cutover. Each is tracked as a TODO in the codebase.
+
+| ID | Severity | Description | File | Pre-staging action |
+|----|----------|-------------|------|--------------------|
+| H-2 | HIGH | Router endpoints have zero auth enforcement — `enforce_seller_context` exists but is never called from router. No `get_current_user` FastAPI Depends exists yet. Gate 6 tenant isolation is untested at the HTTP layer. | `app/pricing/router.py` | Design `get_current_user` dependency (JWT / session token); wire into all 4 endpoints. File as separate story. |
+| H-3 | HIGH | `HttpTargetPricingClient.update_price()` creates a new `httpx.AsyncClient` (new TLS connection) per call — no connection pooling. | `app/pricing/client.py:55` | Refactor to shared client with `lifespan` context or `__aenter__`/`__aexit__`. |
+| M-1 | MEDIUM | Backoff formula missing jitter — spec says `delay = min(base * 2^n + random_jitter(0,1), 300)`. Without jitter, parallel workers (future) will thunderherd. | `app/pricing/worker.py:31` | Add `random.uniform(0, 1)` before `min()` clamp. |
+| M-5 | MEDIUM | `retry_dead_letter()` resets `retry_count=0` — operator can loop indefinitely. Acceptable as intentional operator override but undocumented. | `app/pricing/queue.py:200` | Add `total_attempts` counter that never resets (observability only). |
+| M-6 | MEDIUM | `retry_dead_letter()` allows duplicate pending rows if the same price tuple was re-enqueued normally between dead-lettering and the retry. | `app/pricing/queue.py:186` | Pre-check for existing pending/inflight/failed row with same idempotency key before re-enqueuing dead letter. |
+| L-2 | LOW | Silent no-op in `mark_failed()`/`mark_dead_letter()` when queue_id not found. Should log a warning. | `app/pricing/queue.py:120,133` | Add `logger.warning(...)` on missing row_id. |
+| L-3 | LOW | `_calculate_backoff(base=2.0)` parameter is never overridden — should be module constant. Off-by-one vs spec sequence (first retry is 4s not 2s). | `app/pricing/worker.py:31` | Convert to `_BACKOFF_BASE = 2.0`; adjust call to pass `retry_count - 1` to produce spec sequence. |
+| L-4 | LOW | `Retry-After` header not parsed — spec requires honoring it on 429. | `app/pricing/client.py` | Add `retry_after_seconds` to `PriceUpdateResult`; parse header in `HttpTargetPricingClient`; respect in worker. |
+| L-5 | LOW | `PricingWorker.client` captured at construction — DI override must precede instantiation (undocumented contract). | `app/pricing/worker.py:50` | Add docstring; or refactor to lazy property. |
