+# STORY-013 Feature Spec — Target Pricing Sync (per-item loop)
+
+**Story:** STORY-013
+**Scope:** Medium
+**Phase:** 6 — Design
+**Date:** 2026-04-29
+**Depends on:** STORY-007 (rate limits, currency confirmation), STORY-008 (items must exist in Target)
+**Reused by:** STORY-014 (inventory sync inherits queue pattern)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Overview
+
+Implement Target Plus pricing synchronization via per-item PUT calls. Target prohibits bulk pricing updates — each item requires a separate `PUT /sellers/v1/sellers/{seller_id}/prices/{product_id}` call. This story builds a Postgres-backed job queue (SKIP LOCKED) that drains at the API rate limit, records every PUT outcome to a price history table, and exposes internal FastAPI endpoints for enqueuing price changes and querying sync status.
+
+The queue pattern established here is the canonical per-item loop — STORY-014 (inventory) will reuse the same queue infrastructure with an additional distribution-center dimension.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Target API Contract
+
+**Endpoint:** `PUT /sellers/v1/sellers/{seller_id}/prices/{product_id}`
+**Source:** `target-openapi.yaml` line 751, confidence: verified
+
+### Request Body (Price schema)
+
+| Field | Type | Required | Description |
+|-------|------|----------|-------------|
+| `list_price` | number (double) | Yes | Retail / list price |
+| `offer_price` | number (double) | No | Discounted / sale price |
+| `map_price` | number (double) | No | Minimum Advertised Price |
+
+- Currency: **USD only** (Target Plus is US-only; hardcoded). Column reserved for future `currency` if needed.
+- Content-Type: `application/json`
+
+### Response
+
+| Status | Meaning | Action |
+|--------|---------|--------|
+| 200 | Price updated | Record success in `target_price_history` |
+| 400 | Bad request (malformed body) | Permanent failure — dead-letter, log, alert |
+| 401/403 | Auth failure | Permanent failure — dead-letter, alert operator |
+| 404 | Product not found | Permanent failure — item may not be APPROVED yet (STORY-008 dependency) |
+| 422 | Validation error (e.g., offer > list) | Permanent failure — dead-letter with validation detail |
+| 429 | Rate limited | Retry — honor `Retry-After` header; else exponential backoff |
+| 5xx | Server error | Retry with exponential backoff |
+
+### Rate Limit
+
+- **Default:** 1 request/second (conservative; OQ-3 unresolved until STORY-007 captures actual limit)
+- **Configuration:** `PRICING_RATE_LIMIT_RPS` env var, overridable via DB setting `target_pricing_rate_limit`
+- **Enforcement:** Token bucket in worker; sleep between PUTs to stay under limit
+
+---
+
+## 3. Architecture
+
+### Component Diagram
+
+```
+                          ┌──────────────────┐
+  Operator / Agent ──────>│  FastAPI Router   │
+  (enqueue price change)  │  POST /pricing/   │
+                          │  enqueue          │
+                          └────────┬──────────┘
+                                   │ INSERT
+                                   v
+                          ┌──────────────────┐
+                          │ target_price_queue│  (Postgres)
+                          │ SKIP LOCKED rows  │
+                          └────────┬──────────┘
+                                   │ SELECT FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
+                                   v
+                          ┌──────────────────┐
+                          │  Pricing Worker   │  (asyncio background task)
+                          │  rate-limited     │
+                          │  1 PUT per tick   │
+                          └────────┬──────────┘
+                                   │ PUT /sellers/v1/.../prices/{id}
+                                   v
+                          ┌──────────────────┐
+                          │ Target API        │
+                          │ (staging / prod)  │
+                          └────────┬──────────┘
+                                   │ response
+                                   v
+                          ┌──────────────────────┐
+                          │ target_price_history  │  (Postgres — audit trail)
+                          └──────────────────────┘
+```
+
+### Key Design Decisions
+
+| Decision | Choice | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|-----------|
+| Queue technology | Postgres SKIP LOCKED | Zero new infra; API rate limit makes DB polling irrelevant as bottleneck (Phase 4 analysis score: 4.65/5) |
+| Worker model | Single asyncio background task | One worker, one PUT at a time — matches 1 req/s rate limit; no need for concurrency |
+| Idempotency | Composite unique constraint `(product_id, list_price, offer_price, map_price)` + `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` | Natural fit for per-item PUT; dedupes identical price tuples in-flight |
+| Retry | Exponential backoff, base 2s, max 5 retries, jitter | Industry standard for rate-limited APIs |
+| Dead letter | `status = 'dead_letter'` in queue table | No separate dead-letter table; operator queries `WHERE status = 'dead_letter'` |
+| MAP price source | Operator UI (manual) | No confirmed NetSuite MAP field; `map_price_source` enum for future flexibility |
+| Currency | USD hardcoded | Target Plus is US-only marketplace |
+| Authorization | Single `enforce_seller_context()` dependency | All endpoints validate seller_id ownership through one function |
+
+### Failure Modes
+
+| Dependency | Unavailable Behavior | Rationale |
+|------------|---------------------|-----------|
+| Postgres | Fail-closed (503) — worker stops, enqueue returns 503 | Cannot enqueue or dequeue without DB; no silent data loss |
+| Target API | Fail-closed — worker retries with backoff, then dead-letters | Price writes are critical; never silently skip |
+| Auth token expired | Fail-closed — worker pauses, alerts operator | Cannot send prices without valid auth |
+
+---
+
+## 4. Database Schema
+
+### Table: `target_price_queue`
+
+The inflight job queue. Rows are claimed via `SELECT FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, processed, then marked complete or dead-lettered.
+
+```sql
+CREATE TABLE target_price_queue (
+    id              BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
+    product_id      VARCHAR(64)    NOT NULL,   -- Target TCIN / product identifier
+    seller_id       VARCHAR(64)    NOT NULL,   -- Target seller identifier
+    list_price      NUMERIC(10,2)  NOT NULL,   -- Required by Target API
+    offer_price     NUMERIC(10,2),             -- Optional sale price
+    map_price       NUMERIC(10,2),             -- Optional MAP price
+    map_price_source VARCHAR(16)   NOT NULL DEFAULT 'manual',  -- enum: 'manual', 'netsuite'
+    status          VARCHAR(16)    NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',
+                    -- enum: 'pending', 'inflight', 'complete', 'failed', 'dead_letter'
+    retry_count     SMALLINT       NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
+    max_retries     SMALLINT       NOT NULL DEFAULT 5,
+    next_retry_at   TIMESTAMPTZ,              -- NULL = immediately eligible
+    error_detail    TEXT,                      -- Last error message (for operator review)
+    created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ    NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
+    updated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ    NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
+    claimed_at      TIMESTAMPTZ,              -- When worker picked it up
+
+    -- Idempotency: prevent duplicate inflight entries for same price tuple
+    CONSTRAINT uq_inflight_price
+        UNIQUE (product_id, list_price, offer_price, map_price)
+        -- Note: partial unique index WHERE status IN ('pending','inflight') would be
+        -- more precise but Alembic + SQLAlchemy support for partial uniques is fragile.
+        -- Full unique is acceptable: completed rows are DELETEd after history insert.
+);
+
+CREATE INDEX ix_price_queue_poll
+    ON target_price_queue (status, next_retry_at)
+    WHERE status IN ('pending', 'failed');
+
+CREATE INDEX ix_price_queue_product
+    ON target_price_queue (product_id);
+```
+
+### Table: `target_price_history`
+
+Immutable audit trail. Every PUT attempt (success or failure) is recorded here.
+
+```sql
+CREATE TABLE target_price_history (
+    id              BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
+    product_id      VARCHAR(64)    NOT NULL,
+    seller_id       VARCHAR(64)    NOT NULL,
+    list_price      NUMERIC(10,2)  NOT NULL,
+    offer_price     NUMERIC(10,2),
+    map_price       NUMERIC(10,2),
+    map_price_source VARCHAR(16)   NOT NULL DEFAULT 'manual',
+    http_status     SMALLINT,                 -- Target API response status code
+    response_body   JSONB,                    -- Target API response (for debugging)
+    error_detail    TEXT,                      -- Error message if failed
+    outcome         VARCHAR(16)    NOT NULL,   -- enum: 'success', 'client_error', 'server_error', 'dead_letter'
+    attempted_at    TIMESTAMPTZ    NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
+    duration_ms     INTEGER                    -- Round-trip time in milliseconds
+);
+
+CREATE INDEX ix_price_history_product_time
+    ON target_price_history (product_id, attempted_at DESC);
+
+CREATE INDEX ix_price_history_outcome
+    ON target_price_history (outcome)
+    WHERE outcome != 'success';
+```
+
+### View: `v_pricing_cross_channel`
+
+Cross-channel pricing view joining Target and Amazon pricing data. Enables SC-3 (cross-channel pricing reporting).
+
+```sql
+CREATE VIEW v_pricing_cross_channel AS
+SELECT
+    tph.product_id                          AS target_product_id,
+    tph.list_price                          AS target_list_price,
+    tph.offer_price                         AS target_offer_price,
+    tph.map_price                           AS target_map_price,
+    tph.attempted_at                        AS target_price_updated_at,
+    -- Amazon columns (placeholder — exact table/column names from tech-datawarehouse
+    -- to be confirmed when Amazon pricing tables are available in this DB or via
+    -- foreign data wrapper / cross-DB join)
+    NULL::VARCHAR(64)                       AS amazon_sku,
+    NULL::NUMERIC(10,2)                     AS amazon_your_price,
+    NULL::NUMERIC(10,2)                     AS amazon_list_price,
+    NULL::TIMESTAMPTZ                       AS amazon_price_updated_at
+FROM target_price_history tph
+WHERE tph.outcome = 'success';
+-- NOTE: Full cross-channel join requires SKU mapping table (product_id <-> amazon_sku).
+-- Placeholder until STORY-015 (catalog read sync) provides the mapping.
+-- Phase 8 will implement the view with available columns; Amazon side is stubbed.
+```
+
+### Migration Strategy
+
+- Single Alembic migration: `alembic/versions/YYYYMMDD_HHMM_target_pricing.py`
+- Creates both tables, both indexes, and the view
+- Tables created in server lifespan startup (before background worker starts)
+- Downgrade: drops view, then history table, then queue table (reverse order)
+
+---
+
+## 5. Internal API Design
+
+These are GC-internal FastAPI endpoints — not Target API endpoints. They allow operators and agents to enqueue price changes and monitor sync status.
+
+### Authorization
+
+**Single enforcement point:** `enforce_seller_context(seller_id, current_user)` — a FastAPI `Depends()` callable that validates the current user/agent has access to the given seller_id. All pricing endpoints route through this dependency. No authorization logic exists outside this function.
+
+### `POST /api/v1/pricing/enqueue`
+
+Enqueue one or more price updates for processing.
+
+**Request:**
+
+```json
+{
+    "items": [
+        {
+            "product_id": "12345678",
+            "seller_id": "SELLER_001",
+            "list_price": 19.99,
+            "offer_price": 17.99,
+            "map_price": 15.00,
+            "map_price_source": "manual"
+        }
+    ]
+}
+```
+
+| Field | Type | Required | Validation |
+|-------|------|----------|------------|
+| `items` | array | Yes | 1..100 items per request |
+| `items[].product_id` | string | Yes | Non-empty, max 64 chars |
+| `items[].seller_id` | string | Yes | Must match authenticated seller context |
+| `items[].list_price` | number | Yes | > 0, max 2 decimal places |
+| `items[].offer_price` | number | No | If present: > 0 and <= list_price |
+| `items[].map_price` | number | No | If present: > 0 |
+| `items[].map_price_source` | string | No | Enum: `manual` (default), `netsuite` |
+
+**Responses:**
+
+| Status | Body | Condition |
+|--------|------|-----------|
+| 202 Accepted | `{"enqueued": 3, "deduplicated": 1, "total": 4}` | Items accepted for processing |
+| 400 | RFC 7807 Problem Details | Malformed request |
+| 401 | RFC 7807 Problem Details | Missing/invalid auth |
+| 403 | RFC 7807 Problem Details | Seller context mismatch |
+| 422 | RFC 7807 Problem Details with `field_errors` | Validation failures (e.g., offer > list) |
+| 503 | RFC 7807 Problem Details | Database unavailable |
+
+**Behavior:**
+- Unknown fields: rejected (422) via Pydantic `model_config = ConfigDict(extra="forbid")`
+- Idempotency: duplicate `(product_id, list_price, offer_price, map_price)` tuples already in pending/inflight → `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`, counted as `deduplicated`
+- Not idempotent (POST creates queue entries)
+
+### `GET /api/v1/pricing/status/{product_id}`
+
+Get current pricing sync status for a product.
+
+**Responses:**
+
+| Status | Body | Condition |
+|--------|------|-----------|
+| 200 | `{"product_id": "...", "queue": [...], "last_success": {...}}` | Found |
+| 404 | RFC 7807 Problem Details | No pricing records for product_id |
+| 401/403 | RFC 7807 Problem Details | Auth failure |
+
+**Behavior:**
+- Returns pending/inflight queue entries + most recent successful history entry
+- Resource must exist (404 if no records)
+- Idempotent (GET)
+
+### `GET /api/v1/pricing/dead-letters`
+
+List dead-lettered price updates for operator review.
+
+**Query Parameters:**
+
+| Param | Type | Default | Description |
+|-------|------|---------|-------------|
+| `seller_id` | string | required | Scoped to seller |
+| `limit` | int | 50 | Max 100 |
+| `offset` | int | 0 | Pagination offset |
+
+**Responses:**
+
+| Status | Body | Condition |
+|--------|------|-----------|
+| 200 | `{"items": [...], "total": N}` | Dead-letter list |
+| 401/403 | RFC 7807 Problem Details | Auth failure |
+
+**Behavior:**
+- Idempotent (GET)
+- Returns 200 with empty list if no dead letters (not 404)
+
+### `POST /api/v1/pricing/dead-letters/{id}/retry`
+
+Re-enqueue a dead-lettered item for retry.
+
+**Responses:**
+
+| Status | Body | Condition |
+|--------|------|-----------|
+| 200 | `{"status": "re-enqueued", "queue_id": N}` | Item moved back to pending |
+| 404 | RFC 7807 Problem Details | Dead-letter ID not found |
+| 409 | RFC 7807 Problem Details | Item already re-enqueued (idempotency guard) |
+| 401/403 | RFC 7807 Problem Details | Auth failure |
+
+---
+
+## 6. Error Handling Design
+
+### Error Response Format (RFC 7807)
+
+All error responses use `Content-Type: application/problem+json`:
+
+```json
+{
+    "type": "/problems/validation-error",
+    "title": "Validation Error",
+    "status": 422,
+    "detail": "offer_price (24.99) exceeds list_price (19.99) for product 12345678",
+    "instance": "/api/v1/pricing/enqueue",
+    "field_errors": [
+        {"field": "items[0].offer_price", "message": "must be <= list_price"}
+    ]
+}
+```
+
+### Logged Context on Error
+
+| Field | Logged | Purpose |
+|-------|--------|---------|
+| `operation` | Yes | e.g., `pricing.enqueue`, `pricing.worker.put` |
+| `product_id` | Yes | Identify affected item |
+| `seller_id` | Yes | Identify affected seller |
+| `http_status` | Yes | Target API response code |
+| `retry_count` | Yes | Current retry attempt |
+| `duration_ms` | Yes | Round-trip time |
+| `trace_id` | Yes | Correlation ID for request tracing |
+| `error_class` | Yes | Exception class name |
+
+### NOT Exposed to Callers
+
+- Stack traces (logged internally, never in response body)
+- Internal file paths
+- Database connection strings / credentials
+- Target API auth tokens
+- Raw Target API response bodies (only structured summaries)
+
+### Fallback Behavior
+
+| Dependency | Behavior | Type |
+|------------|----------|------|
+| Postgres unavailable | **Fail-closed** — return 503; worker stops polling | Reject |
+| Target API unavailable | **Fail-closed** — retry with backoff; dead-letter after max retries | Retry then reject |
+| Auth token expired | **Fail-closed** — worker pauses; operator alert | Reject |
+
+---
+
+## 7. Worker Design
+
+### Lifecycle
+
+- Starts as a FastAPI lifespan background task (not a separate process)
+- On startup: ensures `target_price_queue` and `target_price_history` tables exist
+- Polls every 5 seconds (configurable: `PRICING_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS`)
+- Processes one item per tick at rate limit pace
+- On shutdown: gracefully finishes current item, stops polling
+
+### Processing Loop (pseudocode)
+
+```
+while running:
+    async with db.transaction():
+        row = SELECT * FROM target_price_queue
+               WHERE status IN ('pending', 'failed')
+               AND (next_retry_at IS NULL OR next_retry_at <= NOW())
+               ORDER BY created_at ASC
+               LIMIT 1
+               FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
+
+        if row is None:
+            await asyncio.sleep(poll_interval)
+            continue
+
+        UPDATE target_price_queue SET status='inflight', claimed_at=NOW() WHERE id=row.id
+
+    try:
+        response = await target_pricing_client.update_price(
+            seller_id=row.seller_id,
+            product_id=row.product_id,
+            list_price=row.list_price,
+            offer_price=row.offer_price,
+            map_price=row.map_price
+        )
+
+        INSERT INTO target_price_history (outcome='success', http_status=200, ...)
+        DELETE FROM target_price_queue WHERE id=row.id
+
+    except RateLimitError:
+        retry_after = parse_retry_after(response) or exponential_backoff(row.retry_count)
+        UPDATE target_price_queue SET status='failed', retry_count+=1,
+               next_retry_at=NOW()+retry_after WHERE id=row.id
+
+    except PermanentError (400, 401, 403, 404, 422):
+        if row.retry_count >= row.max_retries:
+            UPDATE target_price_queue SET status='dead_letter' WHERE id=row.id
+            INSERT INTO target_price_history (outcome='dead_letter', ...)
+        else:
+            -- 4xx other than 429 are permanent; dead-letter immediately
+            UPDATE target_price_queue SET status='dead_letter' WHERE id=row.id
+            INSERT INTO target_price_history (outcome='client_error', ...)
+
+    except ServerError (5xx):
+        if row.retry_count >= row.max_retries:
+            UPDATE target_price_queue SET status='dead_letter' WHERE id=row.id
+            INSERT INTO target_price_history (outcome='dead_letter', ...)
+        else:
+            backoff = exponential_backoff(row.retry_count)
+            UPDATE target_price_queue SET status='failed', retry_count+=1,
+                   next_retry_at=NOW()+backoff WHERE id=row.id
+            INSERT INTO target_price_history (outcome='server_error', ...)
+
+    await rate_limit_sleep()  -- enforce PRICING_RATE_LIMIT_RPS
+```
+
+### Retry Policy
+
+| Condition | Retryable? | Strategy |
+|-----------|-----------|----------|
+| 429 Rate Limited | Yes | Honor `Retry-After` header; else backoff 2^n seconds + jitter |
+| 5xx Server Error | Yes | Exponential backoff: 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s, 32s (max 5 retries) |
+| 400 Bad Request | No | Immediate dead-letter |
+| 401/403 Auth | No | Immediate dead-letter + operator alert |
+| 404 Not Found | No | Immediate dead-letter (product not approved yet) |
+| 422 Validation | No | Immediate dead-letter with validation details |
+| Network timeout | Yes | Treated as 5xx; retry with backoff |
+
+### Exponential Backoff
+
+```
+delay = min(base * 2^retry_count + random_jitter(0, 1), max_delay)
+base = 2 seconds
+max_delay = 300 seconds (5 minutes)
+```
+
+---
+
+## 8. Implementation Patterns
+
+### Parameter Binding (Postgres via SQLAlchemy + asyncpg)
+
+- All queries use SQLAlchemy Core or ORM with bound parameters (`:name` style)
+- **No f-string interpolation in any SQL**
+- Example: `text("SELECT * FROM target_price_queue WHERE status = :status").bindparams(status="pending")`
+
+### Error Handling Pattern (per adapter)
+
+| Adapter | Exception Type | Handling |
+|---------|---------------|----------|
+| Postgres (asyncpg) | `asyncpg.PostgresError` | Log with operation context; raise 503 to caller |
+| Target API (httpx) | `httpx.HTTPStatusError` | Map status code to retry/permanent per table above |
+| Target API (httpx) | `httpx.TimeoutException` | Treat as retryable server error |
+| Target API (httpx) | `httpx.ConnectError` | Treat as retryable server error |
+
+### Query Generation
+
+- Parameterized only — SQLAlchemy ORM models for queue and history tables
+- Raw SQL only for the `v_pricing_cross_channel` view creation (in migration)
+- All dynamic filters use `.where()` clauses with bound parameters
+
+### Pagination Strategy
+
+- **Application-level only** (SQL `LIMIT`/`OFFSET` on dead-letter listing endpoint)
+- Queue polling: `LIMIT 1` per tick (not paginated — single-item processing)
+- No dual pagination (never both SQL and application pagination)
+
