+
+## 9. Operational Readiness
+
+### Health Checks
+
+| Endpoint | What It Checks | Healthy Response |
+|----------|---------------|------------------|
+| `GET /health` | App is running | `{"status": "ok"}` — 200 |
+| `GET /health/ready` | Postgres reachable + worker running | `{"status": "ready", "db": "ok", "worker": "running"}` — 200; or `{"status": "degraded", ...}` — 503 |
+
+### Metrics (Prometheus format at `/metrics`)
+
+| Metric | Type | Labels | Description |
+|--------|------|--------|-------------|
+| `target_pricing_enqueued_total` | counter | `seller_id` | Items enqueued |
+| `target_pricing_processed_total` | counter | `seller_id`, `outcome` | Items processed (success/client_error/server_error/dead_letter) |
+| `target_pricing_queue_depth` | gauge | `status` | Current queue depth by status |
+| `target_pricing_put_duration_seconds` | histogram | `seller_id` | Target API round-trip latency |
+| `target_pricing_retry_total` | counter | `seller_id` | Retry attempts |
+
+### Structured Logging
+
+- Format: JSON (one object per line)
+- Required fields on every log entry: `timestamp`, `level`, `message`, `trace_id`, `operation`
+- Pricing-specific fields: `product_id`, `seller_id`, `http_status`, `retry_count`, `duration_ms`
+- Correlation: `trace_id` propagated from FastAPI request through worker to history record
+
+### Alerting Conditions
+
+| Condition | Severity | Threshold |
+|-----------|----------|-----------|
+| Dead-letter count > 10 in 1 hour | Warning | Operator review queue |
+| Worker not running (health/ready degraded) | Critical | Page on-call |
+| Target API error rate > 50% in 5 min window | Critical | Page on-call |
+| Queue depth > 1000 (items backed up) | Warning | Investigate rate limit or API outage |
+
